{
  "changelog": "- Introduced the \u201cTaste Protocol\u201d to raise design quality, requiring one deliberate, content-specific design risk (\u201csignature move\u201d) per deck while enforcing strict quality floors.\n- Enhanced user interviewing and source-material fidelity: all slides must be strictly grounded in user-provided content, with no invented or embellished information.\n- Refined workflow: parallelizes only safe prep tasks (e.g., asset processing), never divides core understanding or argument, and documents specific habits to minimize wasted round-trips.\n- Improved design decision-making: every guideline may be deviated from, but only if the deviation is explicitly justified and documented in the design plan.\n- Upgraded build workflow with stricter gatekeeping before slide production, ensuring that only the user can waive the independent critical review after seeing the complete deck.",
